# The workspace is generated output and stays out of the repo — except for
# baselines. A baseline is the reference a run is judged against, so it has to
# be committed: with nothing to compare to, CI captures a baseline from the
# commit under test and compares it against itself, and the check can never
# fail. Ignoring the contents rather than the directory itself is what lets the
# negation below apply — git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is
# excluded. Use the "Generate Baselines" workflow to produce baselines that
# match what a Linux runner renders.
.visual-regression/*
!.visual-regression/baselines/
.visual-regression/baselines/**/versions/
# The benchmark suite is the one case that must NOT have committed baselines.
# ci.yml recaptures them from the clean demo pages with --overwrite on every
# run, immediately before comparing against the ?defect= variants, so a
# committed copy would be overwritten and never read. Leaving them out also
# keeps ~270 dev-machine PNGs (Windows-rendered, useless to a Linux runner) from
# being swept into the repo by `git add .visual-regression/`.
.visual-regression/baselines/bmk-*/
# The quantised ONNX (32MB) is the one model artefact that is versioned, via Git
# LFS, so the CI smoke job can prove the AI path executed. Everything else in
# models/ is 123-304MB and stays out. Re-included explicitly because
# `.visual-regression/*` above excludes the whole directory. See
# docs/adr/0004-ci-gates-detection-the-ai-is-smoke-tested.md.
!.visual-regression/models/
.visual-regression/models/*
!.visual-regression/models/visual_ai.quant.onnx
# The sidecar metadata is required alongside it: _load_legacy_or_hybrid_model
# reads class_names, threshold and image_size from this file, and without it
# falls through to torch.load on a file that is not a pickle. 3KB.
!.visual-regression/models/visual_ai.json
# CI writes junit/coverage/benchmark JSON here and uploads it as an artifact.
# live-eval-summary.json is the exception: it is the published classification
# result (n=500), versioned rather than regenerated per run.
#
# `reports/*` rather than `reports/`: git cannot re-include a path whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the negation below only works if the directory
# itself stays un-excluded — the same reason .visual-regression/* is written
# that way above.
reports/*
!reports/live-eval-summary.json
# The measurement taken before the 2026-08-06 ground-truth labelling fix. ADR
# 0006 reasons about the difference between the two, so the earlier run has to
# remain inspectable rather than being a number quoted from a deleted file.
!reports/live-eval-summary-prelabelfix.json
# The same 500 trials scored under the seven-class rule, kept so the 92.60% the
# README quotes for that taxonomy can be checked rather than taken on trust.
!reports/live-eval-summary-7class-20260809.json
# finetune_on_live_pairs.py trains inside its own workspace root so it can never
# write over the deployed model. Those roots hold materialised run dirs and
# multi-hundred-MB checkpoints — generated output, same as .visual-regression/*.
.visual-regression-*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
.ruff_cache/
.tmp_ai_studio_review/
.tmp_figma_review/
.vscode/
scratch/
sdk/node_modules/
sdk/dist/
dashboard_frontend/node_modules/
dashboard_frontend/dist/
dashboard_frontend/test-results/
dashboard_frontend/playwright-report/
dashboard_frontend/.env
dashboard_frontend/.env.local
dashboard_frontend/.env.*.local
.env
.env.local
*.zip
*.bak
storage.db
storage.db-shm
storage.db-wal

.idea/
# Presentation material lives outside the repo; keep any local copy untracked.
poster/
# Per-machine Claude Code overrides — permissions granted for a one-off cleanup,
# a local model choice. The committed .claude/ files (launch.json, and
# settings.json if one is added) stay shared; this one is personal by design and
# was being tracked, so every local permission change showed up as a repo diff.
.claude/settings.local.json
